# SOUNDNESS R600 — THE GRANDFATHER LIST, AND IT IS A RATCHET, NOT A REGISTRY.
#
# Every name below is a scratchpad directory some row cites as its evidence. They are all DEAD: a
# scratchpad lives in a session-scoped temp dir, so a new session gets a new path and the old one is
# gone. Unlike the 531 dead SHA citations repaired in the R591 era, these are NOT RECOVERABLE — git
# filter-repo leaves a commit-map, a deleted temp directory leaves nothing. There is no --apply for
# this and there never will be.
#
# THE COST IS MEASURED, NOT HYPOTHETICAL. R655 (swift) was re-verified on 2026-09-27 and could not be
# reproduced on FIVE separate binaries, one of them built three weeks BEFORE the row was filed. The row
# says "the two arms above are the whole evidence" and they are not sufficient; what was load-bearing
# lived in a scratchpad that no longer exists. That row is now un-actionable until someone re-derives
# what it was measuring, which is the whole of what this class costs.
#
# So this file exists to stop the NEXT one. `sha-citations.py --check` FAILS on any scratchpad citation
# not listed here. Do not add a line to make a gate pass: put the decisive artefact IN the row instead.
# A path is a courtesy, never the evidence. Removing a line when a row stops citing it is always fine.
